{"cid": "Ugy-2eVuqFr4JChqhId4AaABAg.9yn8Qg1_JlY9ynF4ZkTD9v", "text": "It was a typo. the correct expression is : ZF = 20 - jXc. The rest of calculation and the result are correct.", "time": "2 years ago", "author": "@EngineeringinDepth", "channel": "UCUQ82lJT77tBpMOEoK9D3kQ", "votes": "2", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/uCAitoPYnAbV0otoCRpCUxUH7oTLEwhb0eNkG8XuQiM7VcO0jz1KpwlJIJXAyfo1pQCTvP1DLQ=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": true, "time_parsed": 1703802571.4053}
{"cid": "Ugw38nhtgqNh62E8Dcd4AaABAg.9vbctKJcZkG9vgYrgCwiNy", "text": "The 16 ohm is the Xc (capacitor impedance at 1 Mhz). Please review the video at 1:36", "time": "2 years ago", "author": "@EngineeringinDepth", "channel": "UCUQ82lJT77tBpMOEoK9D3kQ", "votes": "1", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/uCAitoPYnAbV0otoCRpCUxUH7oTLEwhb0eNkG8XuQiM7VcO0jz1KpwlJIJXAyfo1pQCTvP1DLQ=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": true, "time_parsed": 1703802571.588233}
{"cid": "Ugw38nhtgqNh62E8Dcd4AaABAg.9vbctKJcZkG9vggx7WTHOS", "text": " @EngineeringinDepth  thank you..got it..", "time": "2 years ago (edited)", "author": "@michaelmorrison7632", "channel": "UCjhZNHklvqilRBS2C1dev1w", "votes": "0", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_njzoySy4pS-z83M7XbrWlFxX4yZ8hQFb5OqCbOdDQ=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": true, "time_parsed": 1703802571.588834}
{"cid": "Ugz55t_lJ11I24EraYd4AaABAg.9y7u2FbJ_V29y8ljxOmbfy", "text": "A capacitor has [ 1/jCw ] impedance where w = 2πf and f is the operating frequency. When we bring the j from denominator to numerator, then it changes its sign from positive to negative. So, in a short, a capacitance always has a negative sign (-j). In other hand, an inductor always has a +j because its impedance is calculated by [ jLw ]. I hope it helps.", "time": "2 years ago", "author": "@EngineeringinDepth", "channel": "UCUQ82lJT77tBpMOEoK9D3kQ", "votes": "0", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/uCAitoPYnAbV0otoCRpCUxUH7oTLEwhb0eNkG8XuQiM7VcO0jz1KpwlJIJXAyfo1pQCTvP1DLQ=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": true, "time_parsed": 1703802571.770848}
{"cid": "UgwEBBlOhX8l32QKQUx4AaABAg.9wFxX5zYpZK9yMQr9VHIoK", "text": "Thanks for your feedback! I am adding subtitle and commentaries in my recent videos.", "time": "2 years ago", "author": "@EngineeringinDepth", "channel": "UCUQ82lJT77tBpMOEoK9D3kQ", "votes": "0", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/uCAitoPYnAbV0otoCRpCUxUH7oTLEwhb0eNkG8XuQiM7VcO0jz1KpwlJIJXAyfo1pQCTvP1DLQ=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": true, "time_parsed": 1703802571.962008}
